From ed060e9aa05478649556aa32627f09c24e559ad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:07:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] badgeui: ISO 15693 cards load and simulate; an iCLASS
 card stays iCLASS

A user's iCLASS card showed as an ISO 15693 tag in Cards and could not
be loaded or simulated:
- hf search tries ISO 15693 before iCLASS, and an iCLASS card can
  answer both; the search took the first "Valid ... found". iCLASS now
  wins when hf search found it, with its CSN as the UID.
- A dump attached to a card now sets the card's type from its name
  (hf-iclass-, hf-15-, hf-mf-, hf-mfu-), also for cards already in
  cards.tsv: an hf-iclass dump makes the card iCLASS.
- ISO 15693 cards with a dump get what iCLASS has: Load into the
  Proxmark3 (hf 15 eload -f), Simulate (hf 15 sim, typed in the
  Console) and Write to a card (hf 15 restore -f, typed in).
- HF > ISO 15693 and HF > iCLASS gain "Load the dump" (eload with the
  saved card's dump) and "Simulate".

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 16/16 on the host (an ISO 15693 card's options and
their commands, an iCLASS dump on a card saved as ISO 15693, the type
screens' new actions); pm3ui_pm3.c compiled for the badge. The search
change needs a real card: not yet tested on the badge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
